sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: `orbit proof COMMAND`, the first step of stage 3 of the command development pipeline. The author proves one command in the task copy they work in, with the nested fleet that copy already has and no new copy. The Gateway records the intent and the verdicts; Orbit's own Swamp reaches the copy through its Node and runs the runner in it as `agent`, and resets the copy's inner fleet to `base` before every batch. `proof:run` is the CI path.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: proof
  %% kind: proof.verify
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane CP icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  participant CLI as Operator<br/>orbit proof
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant CP as Task copy<br/>agent in the copy
  CLI->>GW: Prove the command<br/>proof COMMAND --group
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - the route needs Gateway access, which no copy holds; a Node with Gateway access names the group
  %%> - the cases come from the copy's own checkout, so they run against the code the author has now, committed or not
  Note over GW: Admit the proof<br/>copy · group · inputs
  %%> What it records:
  %%> - the copy's Incus project and container, its Node as the SSH target, the copy's inner fleet and the cases file; no secret, and no step calls back
  %%> Refuses:
  %%> - a copy whose last completion failed: `tasks.copy_completion_failed`, with its Operation, failed step, error code and the retry `orbit instance:complete ID`
  %%> - an Instance that is not a clone that keeps its nested fleet, such as a Project's default: `proof.copy_fleet_missing`; the reset never runs on it
  %%> - a group without a copy, a copy that is not active or not running, a Project without a nested fleet, a copy turn that may still run, or another operation on the group
  GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>operation ID
  GW->>SW: Start the run<br/>proof-fleet-verify
  SW->>CP: Select the cases<br/>runner plan --lines
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - every runner call goes Node SSH, `incus exec` into the copy, `runuser -u agent`, as a copy turn does; a missing or invalid cases file fails the run here, before the fleet changes
  loop each batch, in the order of swamp/proof/batches.yaml
    SW->>CP: Reset the inner fleet<br/>restore base · start · ready
    %%> Why:
    %%> - the author's fleet may have moved since the copy started, and cases undo nothing, so every batch, the first included, starts from `base`; a copy can prove again
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - the fleet reset of the copy's container, from its Node: stop the three nested containers, restore `base` of each, start them, migrate the nested Gateway forward, wait for a healthy Doctor
    %%> When:
    %%> - before each batch, never after the last: the fleet keeps what the cases left for the author to read, and the next proof resets first
    %%> Fails:
    %%> - a failed reset stops the run: the cases of this batch and of every later batch are `unrun` with cause `infrastructure`
    SW->>CP: Run the batch<br/>setup · cases
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - the batch start state, then each case with its own resources and no undo
    %%> - CLI callers use the checkout device saved in the copy fleet’s `base`; nested commands run as `orbit` with its groups
    %%> - each noninteractive node:converge call in a copy may wait 600 seconds; that wait is separate from the case budget for other work
    %%> - a converge CLI timeout fails that case and stops admission of later cases in the batch; they are unrun with cause infrastructure, because the inner Operation may still hold its locks
    %%> - the reset duration is evidence in the batch result, never a verdict
  end
  Note over SW: Join the verdicts<br/>report step
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - one line a case, in plan order; a case of a batch that did not run is `unrun` with cause `infrastructure`
  alt every case passes
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>verdict per case
    Note over GW: Record the result once<br/>PASS
    GW-->>CLI: PASS per case<br/>timings
  else a case failed or did not run
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>verdict per case
    Note over GW: Record the result once<br/>FAIL
    GW--xCLI: Failed check per case<br/>exit nonzero
    %%> Result:
    %%> - `proof.cases_failed` or `proof.run_failed`; the receipt of each case stays in the copy's evidence directory
  end
